  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assessing the Impact of Climate Change on Women and Girls in Central Asia and Planning Further Actions to Mainstream Gender Equality in Climate Change Education (CCE) and Comprehensive School Safety</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The research project will provide UNESCO and national stakeholders with new knowledge and evidence for future actions on how to increase participation of women and girls in capacity building and policy planning by: 1) conducting research to identify gender vulnerabilities and gaps through the lens of climate change, with aim of integrating gender aspects into climate change education and Comprehensive School Safety; 2) applying research-generated evidence on gender-related aspects to UNESCO&#x2019;s future programme planning; 3) raising awareness about the importance of women and girls participating in activities related to CCE and Comprehensive School Safety.</narrative>
  </description>
